    sha256: fc4496aae0bb510fea99ee047b82bbb00182dd336af8dfb065ef040f3967078f
  body: "# Alternative evidence of incapacity in the legacy guidance\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\n\
    The captured guidance allows other evidence where requiring a doctor’s statement would be unreasonable
    and the alternative is sufficient to show that the person should refrain from work because of a specified
    disease or disablement, with reasonableness considered case by case.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\n\
    The two conditions must be retained together. The selected passages do not make every medical statement
    optional, validate any particular evidence, or transfer this route to ESA, UC or statutory sick pay.
    Existing test results, contact with the claimant and other chapter exceptions still matter.\n\n##
    Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 13101, PDF page 10](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a74dd8b40f0b65f61322dcd/dmgch13.pdf#page=10)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 13: Incapacity for work.\n- [DMG 13160, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a74dd8b40f0b65f61322dcd/dmgch13.pdf#page=11)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 13: Incapacity for work.\n- [DMG 13161, PDF page 11](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a74dd8b40f0b65f61322dcd/dmgch13.pdf#page=11)
    — DMG Vol 3 Ch 13: Incapacity for work.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol3-ch13`: PDF SHA-256 `fc4496aae0bb510fea99ee047b82bbb00182dd336af8dfb065ef040f3967078f`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `1c3e2ae8cf5c3f45273274f24d1bafff88d21a657237c557d555fed53088c931`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The passage requires an individual judgement about reasonableness and sufficient
      evidence rather than acceptance or rejection based solely on document type.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch13/0011
      quote: "13160   Evidence other than on an approved form or from a registered medical practitioner\n\
        \                         1\n        can be accepted if\n\n        1.    it is unreasonable to
        require a doctor's statement and\n\n        2.    the evidence shows that the person should not
        work because of a specific\n              disease or disablement.\n                          \
        \                                                 1 SS (Med Ev) Regs, reg 2(1A)"
      locator: DMG 13160
    - page: page/dmg-vol3-ch13/0011
      quote: "13161   The DM decides what is reasonable in each case. For example, evidence from\n   \
        \     alternative therapists such as chiropractors, osteopaths, etc can be accepted if the\n \
        \       person is usually treated by them as well as, or instead of, a general practitioner."
      locator: DMG 13161
